WEBVTT

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:41.180
<b>Planet Zi</b>

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:41.180
<b>Planet Zi</b>

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:39.980
At the far side of the Milky Way lies Planet Zi.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:47.510
There, metallic lifeforms exist, possessing unparalleled fighting abilities.

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:51.360
Known as Zoids, these beings possess an inborn will to fight.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.850
<b>Guylos Empire</b>

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.850
<b>Guylos Empire</b>

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:55.940
They have been employed as the ultimate weapons

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:54.860
<b>Helic Republic</b>

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:54.860
<b>Helic Republic</b>

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:59.530
in the ongoing war between the Empire and the Republic.

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:06.460
Van, a young Zoid-enthusiast born and raised on this world,

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:12.210
suddenly obtained Sieg, an organoid which has the power to combine with other Zoids.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:15.680
After a fateful encounter with the mysterious girl, Fiine,

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:18.740
he sets out on a journey to discover Fiine's past.

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:21.920
<b>The Battle of Cronos<b>!</b></b>

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:21.920
<b>DATS & Zoids-Anime Present:</b>

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:25.390
<b>DATS & Zoids-Anime Present:</b>

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:25.390
<b>The Battle of Cronos<b>!</b></b>

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:32.650
What are you doing out there?

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:34.670
The Imperial Forces are coming.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.140
Get to a shelter, quickly!

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:37.800
Thanks!

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:40.180
But we're fine!

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:42.830
Don't stay here too long.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:53.890
Van, we should get going, too.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:55.730
He said there will be a battle here.

00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:57.620
You go on ahead.

00:02:57.620 --> 00:02:59.780
I'm going to wait here for Raven.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:03.370
If the Imperial army comes charging in, I'm sure Raven will be there, too.

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:08.600
Yeah, yeah... quit acting tough.

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:10.920
Let's get going!

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:16.720
What are you doing?

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:18.210
I said I'm staying here!

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:21.690
There's no other way, since I don't know where he is!

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:25.850
You know, this won't be the only warzone.

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:28.220
It is just a matter of time before the war spreads to the Republic's capital.

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:31.810
Don't you want to look for clues about Zoid Eve before that?

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:34.940
I'm staying here.

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:40.660
Really... cut it out.

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:42.150
Even if you meet Raven, what will you do?

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:44.600
That's obvious!

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:46.660
How is it obvious?

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:48.740
Will you take him out, just like that?

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:51.410
Like I'm gonna do that!

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:53.750
Then what are you going to do?

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:58.120
What are you going to do?

00:03:58.630 --> 00:03:59.860
See?

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:03.130
He said that, but he never really thought it through.

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:05.600
Van, you really never thought it through?

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:08.520
Shut up!

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:11.820
No matter what, I have to face him again!

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:15.100
I won't move a step from here.

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:19.090
Van.

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:21.780
Can't you talk any sense into this stubborn brat, Irvine?!

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:23.980
Let him do what he wants.

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:25.720
Just let him be. I'm leaving.

00:04:27.050 --> 00:04:28.680
Wait!

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:31.290
I don't want to get involved in a war that has nothing to do with me.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:34.020
What the...? You cold-hearted snake!

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.290
Van.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:41.170
Raven.

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:03.190
Those were Sleepers?

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:04.830
What a disappointment.

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:07.320
Right, Shadow?

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:30.360
Nice job as usual, Raven.

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:32.100
Thanks to you, we can advance smoothly.

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:34.430
I'm not doing this for you.

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:41.620
Who does he think he is?

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:45.410
He couldn't do anything without his Organoid.

00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:48.280
Everyone, back to your stations!

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:48.950
Dismissed!

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:56.980
You have advanced too far.

00:05:56.980 --> 00:06:01.000
On the contrary, Major, your troop is lagging behind schedule.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.560
What are you thinking?

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:06.840
We will not be able to report to Lord Proitzen.

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:11.080
We had a bit of trouble making the rendezvous with the supply unit, but we're all set now.

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:13.970
What about your Iron Kong?

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:16.670
It has just arrived.

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:18.980
We will advance at full speed from now on.

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:20.940
Please wait until I arrive.

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:26.130
I have been ordered to provide backup for Raven.

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:29.400
I must keep up with his pace.

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:34.760
It's fine to kiss Proitzen's feet, but the Republican Forces are not so weak.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:37.080
You will regret it if you underestimate them.

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:43.590
That is why we're combining our troops before attacking Fort Cronos.

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:47.090
And that is my reason for contacting you.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:49.840
I received new orders from command this morning.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:52.340
There has been a change in strategy.

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:56.810
My troop will attack Fort Cronos.

00:06:56.810 --> 00:07:02.350
While yours will stay in reserve until the second attack on Mount Ossa

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:05.510
against the last stronghold of the rebels.

00:07:05.510 --> 00:07:07.070
Those are our updated orders.

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:09.240
What do you mean?

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:11.570
Do you acknowledge?

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:20.240
The fort will be taken by your troop alone.

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:23.870
My forces will stay in reserve until the second attack on Mount Ossa.

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:26.890
We will initiate the plan tomorrow morning.

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:29.760
You can come and watch, if you like.

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:32.720
Yes, I will observe.

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:36.550
My troop alone will be more than enough to take down Fort Cronos.

00:07:39.230 --> 00:07:41.730
And when that's done, you will no longer be needed.

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:48.370
The Republican capital is just a stone's throw away.

00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:50.990
They must be feeling the heat by now.

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:53.760
There's a good chance...

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:58.030
That Fort Cronos is preparing <i>that </i> thing.

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:30.780
Here too?

00:08:39.630 --> 00:08:41.040
Damn it.

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:42.790
This is not what I expected.

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:45.030
There's not a single functioning Gojulas here.

00:08:45.030 --> 00:08:45.490
Hurry up!

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:48.210
The Imperial Forces could attack at any time.

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:50.380
That's Colonel Krueger for you.

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:53.910
Nobody else could come up with such a bold strategy.

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:57.390
But it doesn't change the fact that we're up against the wall.

00:08:57.380 --> 00:09:00.610
That doesn't mean we'll lose.

00:09:00.610 --> 00:09:02.590
We won't let the Imperial Forces have their way.

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:04.020
Yeah.

00:09:05.610 --> 00:09:08.880
So that's where the Imperial Forces are.

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:12.900
My, my... looks like this fortress really is in trouble.

00:09:13.790 --> 00:09:16.900
But what's this "bold strategy?"

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:20.460
What are these guys planning?

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:31.340
Zoids, Zoids...

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:34.220
They don't even know how to use them properly.

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:36.300
Doesn't it piss you off?

00:09:49.430 --> 00:09:51.720
This doesn't work either...

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:53.380
Then how about this?

00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:04.490
Look, look!

00:10:05.070 --> 00:10:06.370
What are you doing?

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:08.490
You are hungry, right?

00:10:08.490 --> 00:10:11.000
If you forget about Raven, I will let you have it.

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:15.590
Like I'm gonna be bribed by food. {"to bribe" has the same pronounciation as "to fish", hence the fishing rod.}

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:29.560
Great catch!

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:32.060
Yahoo!

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:34.480
Hooked in the end.

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:37.080
Listen.

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:39.490
We will leave once you've finished eating.

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:41.900
I didn't hear that.

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:46.570
We will leave as soon as you've finished eating!

00:10:46.570 --> 00:10:47.410
Hear that?

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:48.580
Shut up!

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:50.260
I'm not going. I mean it!

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:01.950
Don't worry about it.

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:05.370
He will fall asleep as soon as he's full.

00:11:05.650 --> 00:11:08.100
Then, we will tie him up.

00:11:08.920 --> 00:11:10.600
So that's why we waited until nightfall.

00:11:21.790 --> 00:11:26.450
The Shield Liger was designed specifically to counter the Saber Tiger.

00:11:26.770 --> 00:11:32.750
Losing to Raven means that I haven't brought out 100% of its fighting ability.

00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:39.010
100%... if I just knew how to use <i>that </i>...

00:12:02.850 --> 00:12:04.520
Are you sure, Irvine?

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:06.490
The Imperial Forces are there?

00:12:06.900 --> 00:12:09.140
Yeah, there's no mistaking it.

00:12:09.140 --> 00:12:11.870
You have to act fast if you want to fight him.

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:14.790
We won't have time once the fort is attacked.

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:16.780
That's true.

00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:18.340
But why did you...?

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:21.050
Just felt like it.

00:12:22.210 --> 00:12:24.330
I owe you one, Irvine.

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:26.050
You are so hard to understand.

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:31.560
You said to just let him be, yet you came back and told him that.

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:34.060
So this is how men are.

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:39.750
Well, if what he said is true, then I'll be gone for a while.

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:42.210
Yeah, yeah. Do whatever you want.

00:12:42.210 --> 00:12:44.820
I'm tired of being your babysitter.

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:47.240
But if things get bad, you'll be rescued by...

00:12:48.550 --> 00:12:49.950
Irvine.

00:12:50.360 --> 00:12:51.080
What? Me?!

00:12:51.570 --> 00:12:53.200
Of course!

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:55.700
That's what you get for telling Van things he didn't need to know.

00:12:55.700 --> 00:12:56.640
Please.

00:12:58.950 --> 00:13:00.820
Like I need your help!

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:04.820
By the way, why are you holding those ropes?

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:18.800
Is it all right to let Van go by himself?

00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:21.450
We just want to find Raven and draw him out.

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:23.400
It's better not to attract too much attention.

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:38.420
Where are you, Raven?

00:13:38.890 --> 00:13:41.670
Looks like Major Schwarz has arrived.

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:43.390
We will get moving first thing in the morning.

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:46.700
This is bad!

00:13:47.170 --> 00:13:49.370
Hey. Deal with that.

00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:51.620
Deal with what?

00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:52.990
There, that.

00:13:52.990 --> 00:13:54.060
What?

00:13:57.030 --> 00:13:59.710
I hear the battle will begin at dawn, but...

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:01.740
Schwarz.

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:04.530
Looks like it's part of Marx's plan to let you do whatever you like.

00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:07.450
Do you know why you are being excluded from the attack?

00:14:08.730 --> 00:14:11.690
If your troop and Major Marx's troop had joined together,

00:14:11.690 --> 00:14:17.210
the Republic might offer a ceasefire after seeing your overwhelming superiority in numbers.

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:20.790
Is that what you were thinking, Major?

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:26.310
That's why you favored the combined strategy. But Proitzen doesn't want a ceasefire.

00:14:26.310 --> 00:14:31.440
The plan was changed probably because he's put pressure on the military brass.

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:35.870
I would have expected you to know this without me explaining it to you.

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:38.020
What are you trying to say?

00:14:39.040 --> 00:14:42.520
It's very simple: Proitzen holds massive power.

00:14:43.010 --> 00:14:48.530
Nobody commands me, as I have  obtained freedom from Proitzen.

00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:52.220
I fight how I want, whenever I want.

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:56.540
I will take down the fort by myself.

00:14:56.860 --> 00:14:58.290
Do you enjoy war?

00:14:58.650 --> 00:15:01.440
The war will not stop as long as the Republic exists.

00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:03.790
That's why I'm going to destroy it.

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:06.700
What crude logic.

00:15:06.700 --> 00:15:08.170
But it does make sense.

00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:13.750
Is there anything else you want to know?

00:15:14.550 --> 00:15:15.680
Then...

00:15:36.560 --> 00:15:37.830
I've found you!

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:39.830
Let's fight one more time!

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:42.080
This guy...

00:15:57.660 --> 00:15:58.970
Let's go, Raven!

00:15:58.970 --> 00:16:02.810
Things didn't end well for me last time, but today it will be different.

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:03.890
I see.

00:16:04.430 --> 00:16:06.180
Your pride as a Zoid pilot?

00:16:06.180 --> 00:16:07.900
You just don't learn.

00:16:08.170 --> 00:16:10.320
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:16:12.710 --> 00:16:16.280
It seems no matter where I go, there's always trash that don't know how to handle a Zoid.

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:18.620
Let's go, Sieg!

00:16:42.090 --> 00:16:44.390
Finally, it's started.

00:16:45.140 --> 00:16:46.400
Van.

00:16:50.240 --> 00:16:54.340
After the barrage by the Red Horns, I will send in the Molga troops.

00:16:55.910 --> 00:17:00.160
We don't know where Raven is! He might get caught in the assault.

00:17:00.430 --> 00:17:03.980
As long as we can ultimately take out the rebels,

00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:07.540
Lord Proitzen won't care much about what happens to Raven.

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:16.770
Commence attack!

00:17:25.030 --> 00:17:28.810
Think of nothing but victory! Take down the rebels!

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:53.340
Damn it.

00:17:59.150 --> 00:18:03.100
He talks big, yet all he can do is get hit!

00:18:07.130 --> 00:18:09.900
Is the best you can do, even using an Organoid?

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:10.940
Shut up!

00:18:12.180 --> 00:18:13.750
The game ends here.

00:18:16.120 --> 00:18:17.530
Damn it!

00:18:48.630 --> 00:18:49.640
Irvine!

00:18:54.080 --> 00:18:57.820
I thought you came to help, but it looks like that's not the case.

00:19:00.130 --> 00:19:00.950
Idiot.

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:17.340
Cut it out, Raven!

00:19:17.910 --> 00:19:20.300
I'm your opponent!

00:19:20.580 --> 00:19:23.600
Damn it. You can do it. Get up.

00:19:26.880 --> 00:19:29.920
This is it! If I can use this...

00:19:29.920 --> 00:19:33.370
What? You're still moving.

00:19:33.370 --> 00:19:36.880
It really makes a difference having an Organoid.

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:40.270
But if you don't know your limits, this is what will happen to you.

00:19:42.190 --> 00:19:44.000
Do you get it?

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:45.120
Raven!

00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:55.200
What?!

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:09.850
He did it!

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:16.900
Shadow!

00:20:29.130 --> 00:20:30.040
Huh?

00:20:35.100 --> 00:20:37.600
Go, Sieg!

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:50.350
Van!

00:21:02.790 --> 00:21:08.030
Everyone of them... are incompetent pilots.

00:21:18.510 --> 00:21:19.840
Damn it!!

00:21:25.980 --> 00:21:27.430
There is no resistance from the enemy.

00:21:28.600 --> 00:21:30.830
They must have gotten scared and retreated.

00:21:30.830 --> 00:21:31.760
It's a trap!

00:21:52.300 --> 00:21:54.980
Jeez... they are all trash.

00:21:56.190 --> 00:21:59.750
Sieg! Sieg!!

00:22:00.910 --> 00:22:03.170
Sieg! Hey, please answer me!

00:22:03.180 --> 00:22:08.320
Sieg, Sieg!!

00:22:07.690 --> 00:22:12.430
Sieg!!

00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:25.300
Preview

00:23:24.430 --> 00:23:26.090
Yo! I'm Van!

00:23:26.090 --> 00:23:28.500
Hey, Sieg, answer me!

00:23:28.500 --> 00:23:30.950
Don't tell me that you have died?

00:23:30.950 --> 00:23:34.850
Just when I don't know what to do, Dr. D appears!

00:23:35.270 --> 00:23:40.610
What? Sieg will wake up if I get a special rock from inside a volcano?

00:23:40.610 --> 00:23:44.900
Okay! If it will help to revive Sieg, I will go anywhere!

00:23:45.260 --> 00:23:47.820
Next time, Zoids episode 14!

00:23:47.820 --> 00:23:49.380
Wake up, Sieg!

00:23:47.820 --> 00:23:52.750
<b>Wake up, Seig!</b>

00:23:49.380 --> 00:23:51.900
Next time, I'll sure be fired up too!
